8	/**
9	 * Public one-click unsubscribe endpoint (RFC 8058 / Gmail-Yahoo bulk rules).
10	 *
11	 * GET  — renders a simple confirmation page. Mail clients that pre-fetch links
12	 *        must NOT trigger a state change, so GET only records the intent when a
13	 *        client explicitly posts; the page shows a one-click confirm form.
14	 * POST  — the `List-Unsubscribe-Post: List-Unsubscribe=One-Click` target. Verifies
15	 *        the HMAC token and writes a GLOBAL Suppression row (reason UNSUBSCRIBE).
16	 *
17	 * No auth. Idempotent — a repeat unsubscribe is a no-op that still reports success.
18	 * We never reveal whether a token maps to a real contact.
19	 */
